parameters.text:
=You are triaging an incoming email.

Pick exactly one category from this list:
{{ $json.Categories }}

Email:
From: {{ $('On New Email').item.json.from }}
Subject: {{ $('On New Email').item.json.subject }}
Body: {{ $('On New Email').item.json.snippet }}

Knowledge base available to answer from:
{{ $json.KnowledgeBase }}

Return ONLY raw JSON, no code fences, no commentary, in exactly this shape:
{"category": "one category from the list above", "confidence": 0-100, "canAnswerFromKnowledgeBase": true or false, "summary": "one line on what they actually want", "reasonIfEscalating": "short reason a human should handle this, or empty string"}

confidence is how certain you are about the category.
canAnswerFromKnowledgeBase is true ONLY if the knowledge base above genuinely contains what is needed to answer them. If they are asking about something it does not cover, that is false - do not guess.

parameters.jsCode:
const cfg = $('Triage Config').first().json;
const email = $('On New Email').item.json;
const raw = String($input.item.json.text || '').trim();

let cleaned = raw.replace(/^```(?:json)?/i, '').replace(/```\s*$/, '').trim();
const s = cleaned.indexOf('{');
const e = cleaned.lastIndexOf('}');
if (s !== -1 && e > s) cleaned = cleaned.slice(s, e + 1);

let p = null;
try {
  p = JSON.parse(cleaned);
} catch (err) {
  p = null;
}

const threshold = Number(cfg.ConfidenceThreshold) || 70;
const toList = v => String(v || '').toLowerCase().split(',').map(x => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);
const escalateCats = toList(cfg.EscalateCategories);
const ignoreCats = toList(cfg.IgnoreCategories);

const category = p && p.category ? String(p.category).trim() : 'unknown';
const confidence = p && typeof p.confidence === 'number' ? p.confidence : 0;
const canAnswer = p ? p.canAnswerFromKnowledgeBase === true : false;
const summary = p && p.summary ? String(p.summary) : 'Classifier returned no usable summary.';
const modelReason = p && p.reasonIfEscalating ? String(p.reasonIfEscalating) : '';

const cat = category.toLowerCase();

let outcome;
let reason = '';

if (ignoreCats.includes(cat)) {
  outcome = 'ignore';
  reason = 'Category "' + category + '" is on the ignore list.';
} else if (!p) {
  outcome = 'escalate';
  reason = 'The classifier returned output that could not be read as JSON.';
} else if (escalateCats.includes(cat)) {
  outcome = 'escalate';
  reason = 'Category "' + category + '" always goes to a human.';
} else if (confidence < threshold) {
  outcome = 'escalate';
  reason = 'Low confidence: ' + confidence + '% against a ' + threshold + '% threshold.';
} else if (!canAnswer) {
  outcome = 'escalate';
  reason = 'The knowledge base does not cover this question.';
} else {
  outcome = 'draft';
}

if (modelReason && outcome === 'escalate') {
  reason = reason + ' ' + modelReason;
}

return {
  json: {
    outcome,
    category,
    confidence,
    canAnswer,
    summary,
    reason: reason.trim(),
    from: email.from || '',
    subject: email.subject || '',
    snippet: email.snippet || '',
    threadId: email.threadId || '',
    messageId: email.id || ''
  }
};

parameters.text:
=Draft a reply to this email.

Category: {{ $json.category }}
What they want: {{ $json.summary }}

Knowledge base - your ONLY source of facts:
{{ $('Triage Config').first().json.KnowledgeBase }}

Original email:
From: {{ $json.from }}
Subject: {{ $json.subject }}
Body: {{ $json.snippet }}

Rules:
- Answer only from the knowledge base. Never invent a price, policy, date, or commitment.
- Match the category: a sales enquiry gets warmth and a next step, a support question gets a direct answer.
- Short. No corporate padding, no "thank you for reaching out".
- Output only the reply body - no subject line, no signature.

